Wrong (B): DFL depends directly on interest expense relative to EBIT, not asset composition; different debt levels produce different DFL values.
Wrong (C): Higher DFL amplifies both gains and losses; it increases risk because earnings volatility is magnified, not reduced.
Wrong (D): DFL and interest coverage are mathematically related — they are reciprocal measures of the same underlying leverage risk under ASC 470 debt frameworks.$EXPL$
